  "question": "Does one ordinary recovery notice preserve final quality and lower complete task cost; does factual reobservation feedback improve over a generic review notice?",
  "treatment": "Only the first qualifying boundary can offer a notice for the next model input. None/generic/factual share the full observation monitor and ordinary unlimited reasoning. No API replacement, blocking or result caching.",
  "comparison_scope": "Four previously known tasks; one task contains monitored Spotify reads. Three new from-start conditions each. All prior outcomes and missing usages are preserved; no heldout requirements read.",
  "common_controls": "Same public task/world, typed results, Python exceptions, all returned reasoning, persistent Python, public schemas, residual output reservation, numeric token/API budgets, canonical transport references, first request cold then warm prefix caching.",
  "order_rule": "Task1 none/generic/factual; task2 generic/factual/none; task3 factual/none/generic; task4 none/generic/factual. World42, model57+call index, one repetition, no threshold or seed search.",
  "cache_rule": "First model request cache_prompt=false and measured cache_n=0/prompt_n=full input are required. Later requests use true. Timing and numerical nondeterminism remain; identical seeds do not guarantee identical trajectories.",
  "budget_rule": "Each cell 80 generations,450000 logical input+output tokens,1800 work seconds; output4096,context65536,reasoning -1,call timeout600 bounded by task time,API160 photo/80 other. Setup120/cleanup180/idle60/evaluation180. Twelve cells reserve960 generations,5400000 tokens,1200 API requests; owned server32400 seconds. Actual usage is reported separately.",
  "failure_rule": "Preserve all attempts. Unknown terminal model usage ends the cell with no response execution or retry. If API effects and cleanup are known, wait<=60s for the same idle server, independently evaluate once and continue the fixed next cell. Unknown API effects, cache mismatch, initialization/runtime/cleanup/evaluation failure, changed server or insufficient lease stops the batch. Never impute missing usage as zero.",
  "primary_cost": "All newly generated full logical input+output tokens from task start, including reasoning, control notices, failed attempts and recovery. Unknown terminal use prevents an exact task total. Also report cached/noncached input, output, model and API calls, work/setup/cleanup/evaluation/model-load/server residency wall separately. No tokens-to-money or time equivalence.",
  "primary_quality": "One official final task-success boolean per frozen cell, with no evaluator feedback returned to the model. No hidden criteria or individual answers inspected.",
  "analysis_rule": "Retain all twelve planned cells, unknown usage, unevaluated and unattempted states. Compare all three pairs with paired-success, both-failed and discordant contributions. Report every notice candidate, offered/supplied/dispatched distinction and the three shadow comparisons. Inspect differences only after cohort closure.",
  "development_gate": "All12 independently evaluated, known terminal usage, clean audit, no per-task success loss, at least one both-successful task, strictly lower aggregate logical tokens. Factual-notice benefit also requires both factual pair gates and at least one generic/factual task with an actually dispatched notice at the same call and identical pre-notice normalized history+budget input hash. No novelty/general-quality/acceptance claim.",
